    "https://westlibertyuniversity.bamboohr.com/careers/276": {
      "title": "West Liberty University - College of Liberal and Creative Arts - Adjunct Openings",
      "description": "West Liberty University - College of Liberal and Creative Arts - Adjunct Openings. Department: Faculty & Adjunct Positions. Temporary. Welcome to West Liberty University! Mission Statement: West Liberty University, established in 1837, was the first institution of higher education in West Virginia. We are a dynamic, inclusive, student-centered community that cultivates scholarly exploration, experiential learning, creative expression, and global citizenship. The Opportunity: If you are passionate about teaching, possess relevant expertise, and are eager to contribute to the academic excellence of our institution, we encourage you to explore our regularly updated adjunct job openings . When submitting your application, kindly specify the desired position for consideration by responding to the corresponding prompt in the application questionnaire. Minimum Requirement: Master's degree in related field. Specific requirements listed with job title below. Please contact hr@westliberty.edu with specific position requirements. College of Liberal and Creative Arts Adjunct Art Therapy and Counseling Job Description The Department of Art Therapy and Counseling is seeking adjunct faculty member for graduate programs: Art Therapy and Counseling and Clinical Mental Health Counseling. Duties & Responsibilities The successful candidate will be responsible for teaching courses in the graduate programs as assigned. When teaching practicum/internship courses, the faculty member will also assess student performance and competency throughout the duration of and at the end of the practicum/internship. The successful candidate will possess credentials to teach a wide range of art therapy and/or counseling courses including addictions counseling. Other responsibilities may be assigned by the Chair and/or Dean of the College as needed. Qualifications The successful candidate will possess a minimum of a Doctorate degree and be knowledgeable in art therapy and/or counseling course content and effective in teaching assigned subjects. Licensed mental health provider and at least five years’ experience as an art therapist and/or counselor in clinical practice. If teaching art therapy courses, the candidate must also possess national certification in the field of art therapy, ATR-BC. At least two years’ experience teaching at the University level. This is an adjunct position, and salary will be commensurate with experience. Why you should apply: Free use of the Wellness facilities and free admission into all WLU events with your employee Topper Card. West Liberty University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and welcomes applications from all interested individuals. Individuals who need assistance in the application process may contact Human Resources at hr@westliberty.edu. For more information about living in the Wheeling area please visit Wheeling: Live Here - Weelunk West Liberty University does not sponsor work visas. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States. Successfully passing a background screening report is required for final employment. West Liberty University is a tobacco free campus."
