    "https://westlibertyuniversity.bamboohr.com/careers/369": {
      "title": "Trades Specialist-Casual",
      "description": "Trades Specialist-Casual. Department: Administration & Staff Positions. Casual. Welcome to West Liberty University! Mission Statement: West Liberty University is a public university with a rich history of providing students with a comprehensive education from undergraduate to graduate degrees. Through experiential learning and personalized support, we empower students toward scholarly exploration, creative expression, and economic opportunity. The Opportunity: West Liberty University is seeking applications for Casual Trades Specialist. The Casual Trades Specialist will assist with the execution and completion of construction and renovation projects. This role involves a variety of carpentry duties as well as supporting the Physical Plant in ensuring the timely and efficient delivery of projects on campus. The ideal candidate will possess a solid understanding of carpentry, construction processes, and safety practices. This Position is a Casual Part-Time Position. An as needed type of Position. Essential Functions of the position: Support the Physical Plant with daily operations, project scheduling, and resource allocation for construction projects. Carpentry Work: Perform a variety of carpentry tasks, including but not limited to framing, installing doors and windows, building and installing cabinets, trim work, and other wood-based projects. Prepare and organize construction sites, including the safe handling and storage of materials. Blueprints and Plans: Review construction plans and blueprints with the Project Manager to ensure that carpentry work meets design specifications and standards. Material Management: Assist in managing and tracking materials required for carpentry tasks, ensuring proper usage and minimizing waste. Safety Compliance: Follow all safety guidelines and regulations while working on-site to ensure a safe work environment for all staff and contractors. Tool Maintenance: Maintain and properly store tools and equipment, ensuring they are in good working condition. Collaboration: Work closely with other tradespeople (electricians, plumbers, etc.) and contractors to ensure the smooth progress of construction projects. Progress Reporting: Assist with the preparation of progress reports, providing updates on carpentry-related work and tasks. Quality Control: Inspect completed carpentry work to ensure high-quality craftsmanship and that all work is in compliance with code. Education & Experience Requirements: A high school diploma or GED is required. Trade school or relevant experience in the field of carpentry is required. Clean Driving Record Skills/Abilities: Communication proficiency Adaptability Strategic Thinking Why you should apply: Free use of the Wellness facilities and free admission into all WLU events with your employee Topper Card. For more information about living in the Wheeling area please visit https://weelunk.com/live-here/ West Liberty University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and welcomes applications from all interested individuals. Individuals who need assistance in the application process may contact Human Resources at hr@westliberty.edu. West Liberty University does not sponsor work visas. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States. Successfully passing a background screening report is required for final employment. West Liberty University is a tobacco free campus."
