    "https://westlibertyuniversity.bamboohr.com/careers/413": {
      "title": "Faculty Construction Management",
      "description": "Faculty Construction Management. Department: Faculty & Adjunct Positions. Full-Time. Welcome to West Liberty University! Mission Statement: West Liberty University, established in 1837, was the first institution of higher education in West Virginia. We are a dynamic, inclusive, student-centered community that cultivates scholarly exploration, experiential learning, creative expression, and global citizenship. The Opportunity: West Liberty University's Gary E. West College of Business is seeking applications for a Construction Management faculty member. The Gary E. West College of Business seeks a dynamic and experienced professional to lead the design, launch, and growth of a four‑year Bachelor’s degree program in Construction Management. This role provides academic leadership across curriculum development, accreditation, teaching, and industry engagement, while contributing broadly to the mission and service commitments of the college and university. The successful candidate will oversee curriculum design and delivery in both online and on‑ground formats; guide the program through institutional, HLC, and ACCE approval and accreditation processes; and teach undergraduate courses aligned with their professional expertise. This position also plays a vital role in faculty governance, assessment and continuous improvement, student recruitment and success, and partnerships with industry. The individual will actively engage in service to the school, college, profession, and community; support diverse learners; collaborate with faculty and staff; and serve as a liaison to professional practice. Additional responsibilities may be assigned by the Dean to support the strategic goals and success of the College of Business. This position is a 9-month tenure track position. Essential Functions of the position: Curriculum development Student advisement Online Instruction Participate in activities related to student recruitment and retention Education & Experience Requirements: Lead the writing and development of a 4-year bachelor's degree curriculum in construction management; Guide the program through college curriculum approvals, HLC program approval, and ACCE accreditation; Lead the development and implementation of the program courses in both the online and on ground formats; Develop and maintain strong partnerships with local, regional, and national construction industry stakeholders to support program growth, experiential learning opportunities, and an engaged advisory board. Teach undergraduate courses in the College of Business in alignment with their experience; Engage in service to the school, college, profession, and community, including: Participation in curriculum development, implementation, evaluation/assessment, and program improvement Participation in accreditation processes at the college and university level Participation in faculty governance by serving on college and university committees and workgroups Participation in the recruitment and selection of qualified faculty and staff within the college Participation in the recruitment and admission of students Participation in College of Business and WLU activities and celebrations Serve as a programmatic liaison to professional practice and industry partners Support the learning needs and success of students from diverse backgrounds Contribute to the success of the College of Business by performing other duties as assigned by the Dean of the College of Business Ideal Candidate Will : Possess a terminal degree in construction management or closely related field from an accredited institution. This position is a tenure track position. Possess demonstrable relevant experience in construction or a comparable industry. Possess collaborative skills to work as part of the College of Business. Possess the ability to manage tasks and processes including developing and implementing new course content in both the on-ground and online formats. Participate with student organizations and/or mentor student organizations. Collaborate with other disciplines and interact with the industry, including participation in or leadership of service learning or other experiential learning projects. Communicate effectively, work cooperatively with students, faculty, staff, and administrators, conduct themselves professionally, and perform appropriate service functions at the department, school, and college levels. Excellent interpersonal, written, graphic, and oral communication skills. Professional certifications or licenses related to the construction industry Optimal Qualifications: Experience in developing, administering or teaching in an ACCE accredited CM program Knowledge of the program approval and accreditation processes within the higher education environment. Application Requirements: Letter of application Curriculum vitae Evidence of teaching effectiveness: course evaluations and sample syllabi Contact information for three professional references. Anticipated Faculty Appointment Date: Fall 2026 A faculty member is expected to participate in continuous improvement in the areas of teaching, professional development, and service to the University and community. Salary will be commensurate with experience. Why you should apply: For the academic year employees, their dependents, and spouses are eligible for a 100% waiver for undergraduate tuition and only employees are eligible for 50% waiver for graduate tuition for certain programs. Free use of the Wellness facilities and free admission into all WLU events with your employee Topper Card. For more information about living in the Wheeling area please visit Wheeling: Live Here - Weelunk West Liberty University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and welcomes applications from all interested individuals. Individuals who need assistance in the application process may contact Human Resources at hr@westliberty.edu. West Liberty University does not sponsor work visas. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States. Successfully passing a background screening report is required for final employment. West Liberty University is a tobacco free campus."
    },
    "https://westlibertyuniversity.bamboohr.com/careers/416": {
      "title": "Recording Engineer (Casual)",
      "description": "Recording Engineer (Casual). Department: Administration & Staff Positions. Temporary. Welcome to West Liberty University! Mission Statement: West Liberty University is a public university with a rich history of providing students with a comprehensive education from undergraduate to graduate degrees. Through experiential learning and personalized support, we empower students toward scholarly exploration, creative expression, and economic opportunity. The Opportunity: West Liberty University is seeking applications for a recording engineer on an as need basis. The Department of Music & Theatre seeks to hire recording engineers to run sessions in our recording studio on a temporary contractual basis. Please submit a resume and at least one letter of recommendation. Experience with Pro Tools software is required. Successful candidates will undergo an orientation in the studio prior to working any sessions. NOTE: This is a parttime (casual) position as needed on campus. Essential Functions of the position: Recording engineers at WLU are expected to run every aspect of a recording session they are assigned to and follow all studio, department, and university procedures Duties include, but are not necessarily limited to, audio recording, tracking, signal processing, mixing, and mastering. Education & Experience Requirements: Recording engineers at WLU are required to have a Bachelor of Music degree in Music Technology, a bachelor's degree in audio engineering (or similar) from a different university, or significant professional experience Skills/Abilities: Required proficiencies: ProTools software, the care and use of microphones and microphone-related equipment, the proper use and maintenance of all studio equipment including, but not limited to, cables, patchbays, preamps, direct boxes, computers, monitors, displays, hard drives, and instruments. Preferred skills: Mixing and post-production. Why you should apply: Free use of the Wellness facilities and free admission into all WLU events with your employee Topper Card. For more information about living in the Wheeling area please visit Wheeling: Live Here - Weelunk West Liberty University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and welcomes applications from all interested individuals. Individuals who need assistance in the application process may contact Human Resources at hr@westliberty.edu. West Liberty University does not sponsor work visas. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States. Successfully passing a background screening report is required for final employment. West Liberty University is a tobacco free campus."
    },
    "https://westlibertyuniversity.bamboohr.com/careers/426": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach Track",
      "description": "Assistant Coach Track. Department: Administration & Staff Positions. Part-Time. Welcome to West Liberty University! Mission Statement: West Liberty University is a public university with a rich history of providing students with a comprehensive education from undergraduate to graduate degrees. Through experiential learning and personalized support, we empower students toward scholarly exploration, creative expression, and economic opportunity. The Opportunity: West Liberty University is seeking applications for an Assistant Coach Track. The Assistant Coach Track under the guidance of the Head Coach, the assistant performs responsible program building tasks including planning, coaching, recruiting, managing and supporting the Track program. The Assistant Coach is also responsible for managing various aspects of the track team, which could include but are not limited to strength and conditioning, practicing, scheduling, and student athlete retention. Job responsibilities require the ability to organize work effectively, conceptualize and prioritize objectives and exercise independent judgement based on an understanding of organizational policies and objectives. This position exercises judgment in prioritizing, planning, and organizing own work within time, process, and results requirements; has some flexibility to modify workflow based on need and circumstances. Decisions made address non-routine questions and situations, requiring investigation and/ or research of precedents. This position is a Part-time non-benefits eligible position. Essential Functions of the position: Assist the Head Track & Field Coach with the planning, organization, and implementation of the track & field program. Assist with conducting practices, including warm-ups, drills, conditioning, event-specific instruction, and skill development. Provide coaching and instruction to student-athletes in assigned track and/or field events. Assist with developing training plans and workouts appropriate to student-athletes’ abilities and competitive schedules. Provide appropriate supervision and instruction to student-athletes during practices, competitions, travel, and team activities. Assist with meet preparation, event entries, equipment setup, and other competition-day responsibilities. Attend and assist with home and away competitions as assigned by the Head Coach. Promote student-athlete development, sportsmanship, teamwork, accountability, and academic success. Monitor and reinforce compliance with university, conference, and applicable NCAA rules, policies, and procedures. Assist with recruiting activities, including identifying prospective student-athletes and communicating with recruits as permitted by applicable rules. Assist with maintaining team and equipment organization, including proper care and inventory of track & field equipment. Communicate effectively with the Head Coach, student-athletes, athletics staff, and other university personnel. Support the overall goals and mission of the university and Department of Athletics. Perform other coaching-related duties as assigned by the Head Coach or Director of Athletics. Education & Experience Requirements: Bachelor's degree in a related field One year of relevant to high school, college or junior college coaching experience One year of Collegiate coaching experience Skills/Abilities: Knowledge, skills required in the area of collegiate athletics Ability to work with limited supervision Excellent computer skills Knowledge of database management Knowledge of email and mail merge programs Good presentation skills Ability to multitask Perform all duties assigned by the head coach Why you should apply: Free use of the Wellness facilities and free admission into all WLU events with your employee Topper Card. For more information about living in the Wheeling area please visit Wheeling: Live Here - Weelunk West Liberty University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and welcomes applications from all interested individuals. Individuals who need assistance in the application process may contact Human Resources at hr@westliberty.edu. West Liberty University does not sponsor work visas. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States. Successfully passing a background screening report is required for final employment. West Liberty University is a tobacco free campus."
    },
    "https://westlibertyuniversity.bamboohr.com/careers/436": {
      "title": "Accounting Assistant",
      "description": "Accounting Assistant. Department: Administration & Staff Positions. Full-Time. West Liberty University | West Liberty, West Virginia Help keep the University moving forward—one accurate transaction at a time. At West Liberty University, accounting is about more than processing numbers. It is about helping departments, faculty, staff, and vendors navigate financial processes accurately, efficiently, and responsibly. We are seeking an Accounting Assistant who combines exceptional customer service with strong attention to detail, sound judgment, and the confidence to uphold established policies and procedures. This is an ideal opportunity for someone who genuinely enjoys helping people—but also understands that good service sometimes means explaining why a process must be followed. The Accounting Assistant supports a variety of institutional accounting functions, including Accounts Payable, Travel, P-Card administration, vendor maintenance, and routine financial transactions. This position serves as a resource to departments across the University and plays an important role in ensuring transactions are properly documented, accurately coded, and compliant with University policies and procedures. Why You Should Apply If you are someone who enjoys solving problems, helping people, and making sure things are done correctly , this could be the position for you. You will have the opportunity to: Become an important resource to departments and employees across the University. Build expertise in higher education accounting and financial processes. Work with a variety of financial transactions, systems, vendors, and University departments. Develop strong knowledge of Accounts Payable, Travel, P-Card administration, and institutional financial procedures. Help employees understand financial requirements and find solutions when transactions don't go as planned. Join a team where accuracy, accountability, professionalism, and service all matter. This position is particularly well suited to someone who can be helpful without being easily pressured . You should be comfortable explaining policies, asking questions, requesting missing documentation, and holding firm to established procedures—even when the person you're working with would prefer a different answer. Who You Are You are a customer-service-minded problem solver who pays attention to the details . You know that providing excellent service doesn't always mean saying \"yes.\" Sometimes, the best service is helping someone understand what is required, explaining why a policy exists, and working with them to find a compliant solution. The ideal candidate is: Service-oriented. You enjoy working with people and approach questions and problems with patience and professionalism. Confident and consistent. You can communicate requirements clearly and professionally and are comfortable enforcing established policies and procedures. Detail-driven. You notice discrepancies, missing documentation, coding errors, and inconsistencies before they become bigger problems. A problem solver. When something doesn't look right, you investigate rather than simply passing it along. Diplomatic but firm. You can maintain positive relationships while still holding employees and departments accountable to established processes. Organized. You can manage multiple transactions, deadlines, questions, and priorities without losing track of the details. A clear communicator. You can explain financial requirements to people who may have little or no accounting background. A team player. You understand that accounting is a service function and that strong working relationships are essential to getting the job done. Trustworthy and discreet. You will regularly work with confidential financial and employee information. What You'll Do As an Accounting Assistant, you will provide day-to-day accounting and administrative support across several important University functions. Customer Service & Department Support Serve as a knowledgeable resource to faculty, staff, departments, vendors, and other University constituents regarding routine accounting questions and processes. Respond to questions and resolve routine issues while escalating more complex matters when appropriate. Explain University policies and financial procedures clearly and professionally. Research issues and work with departments to obtain missing information or resolve discrepancies. Accounts Payable & Vendor Support Process, code, and enter invoices, receipts, check requests, and other Accounts Payable transactions. Review transactions for accuracy, appropriate documentation, and compliance with University policies and contractual requirements, when applicable. Work with regular vendors to place and verify orders and track invoices. Create new vendor accounts and process vendor updates within the institutional system. Research lost payments and other payment-related issues. Travel & Expense Processing Audit, verify, and process travel expense reports. Review travel documentation for accuracy and compliance with institutional policies. Research discrepancies and work with departments to obtain the information necessary to process reimbursements accurately and efficiently. P-Card Administration Review and process P-Card transactions based on departmental budgets, established policies, and P-Card limits. Research rejected or unusual charges, including those resulting from budget errors. Train P-Card holders and maintain required training documentation and compliance. Financial Systems & Reporting Use the University's financial systems to process and post routine accounting transactions, including travel reimbursements, invoices, check requests, and P-Card charges. Maintain accurate records and documentation. Identify, research, and resolve inconsistencies in financial transactions. Perform other related duties as assigned. Education & Experience Required: Associate degree, vocational/technical degree, or equivalent education in Accounting, Finance, Business, or a related field. 1–2 years of directly related work experience. Preferred: 2–3 years of directly related accounting, finance, accounts payable, or administrative experience. Experience working with financial or enterprise resource planning (ERP) systems. Experience in a higher education or similarly regulated environment. Skills & Abilities The successful candidate will demonstrate: Knowledge of basic accounting principles and practices. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. Exceptional attention to detail and accuracy. The ability to identify, research, and resolve accounting discrepancies. The ability to interpret financial information and consistently apply established policies and procedures. Strong organizational and time-management skills. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. The ability to explain financial information and institutional requirements to individuals without an accounting background. The ability to learn and effectively use Banner, Oasis, Microsoft Word, Excel, and other institutional systems. The ability to handle confidential information with discretion. A professional, approachable demeanor and commitment to excellent customer service. The confidence to uphold institutional policies and procedures while maintaining positive working relationships. The ability to establish and maintain effective relationships with students, faculty, staff, vendors, and other University constituents. The Bottom Line We're looking for someone who can be both the friendly face of Accounting and the person who makes sure the rules are followed. If you enjoy helping people, solving problems, catching the details others miss, and bringing consistency and accountability to financial processes, we would like to hear from you. Additional Information: West Liberty University offers generous benefits, including approximately 2 days of annual leave (vacation) per month and 12-13 paid holidays. Visit the WLU Benefit Page for more details: https://westliberty.edu/human-resources/employee-benefits For the academic year employees, their dependents, and spouses are eligible for a 100% waiver for undergraduate tuition and only employees are eligible for 50% waiver for graduate tuition for certain programs. Free use of the Wellness facilities and free admission into all WLU events with your employee Topper Card. For more information about living in the Wheeling area please visit Wheeling: Live Here - Weelunk West Liberty University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and welcomes applications from all interested individuals. Individuals who need assistance in the application process may contact Human Resources at hr@westliberty.edu . West Liberty University does not sponsor work visas. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States. Successfully passing a background screening report is required for final employment. West Liberty University is a tobacco free campus."
    },
    "https://westlibertyuniversity.bamboohr.com/careers/438": {
      "title": "Admissions Events Coordinator",
      "description": "Admissions Events Coordinator. Department: Administration & Staff Positions. Full-Time. West Liberty University | West Liberty, West Virginia Create Memorable Experiences. Inspire Future Hilltoppers. West Liberty University is seeking an energetic, student-centered professional to join our Enrollment Services team as an Admissions Events Coordinator . This highly visible position plays a vital role in helping prospective students and their families discover all that WLU has to offer through engaging, personalized campus visit experiences. As the Admissions Events Coordinator, you will oversee every aspect of the campus visitation program, from individual tours and group visits to large-scale recruitment events. You'll serve as a key ambassador for the University, helping students envision themselves as part of the Hilltopper community while leading and mentoring our Student Ambassador team. If you are passionate about higher education, enjoy event planning, thrive in a fast-paced environment, and love creating meaningful experiences for others, we encourage you to apply. What You'll Do Design and coordinate personalized campus visits, tours, and special event experiences for prospective students, families, and groups. Lead, train, and supervise the WLU Student Ambassador Program. Plan, organize, and participate in admissions recruitment events both on and off campus. Serve as the primary point of contact for visitors throughout their campus experience. Conduct post-visit conversations with students and families, providing guidance and connecting them with appropriate campus resources. Utilize CRM technology to manage visitor communications, track participation, and support recruitment initiatives. Collaborate with faculty, staff, students, and departments across campus to create welcoming and impactful visit experiences. Contribute to the University's enrollment goals by creating exceptional first impressions for future students. Qualifications Required Bachelor's degree in a related field. Minimum of two years of relevant experience, including student leadership, admissions, recruitment, customer service, marketing, event planning, student affairs, or related experience. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple projects and deadlines. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications. Ability to work occasional evenings and weekends for recruitment and special events. Preferred Master's degree in a related field. Experience in higher education, admissions, recruitment, enrollment management, or marketing. Experience utilizing CRM systems, databases, or Banner. Demonstrated success in event planning, relationship building, or student engagement initiatives. What Makes You Successful in This Role? You are: A natural relationship builder who enjoys connecting with students and families. Enthusiastic, outgoing, and passionate about higher education. Detail-oriented with exceptional organizational skills. Comfortable speaking with groups and representing the University. A collaborative team player who enjoys working across departments. Creative and committed to delivering outstanding customer service and event experiences. Why Join West Liberty University? At West Liberty University, you'll find a supportive campus community, meaningful work, and excellent benefits. Benefits Include: Approximately 24 days of annual leave per year 12-13 paid holidays annually Comprehensive benefits package 100% undergraduate tuition waiver for eligible employees, spouses, and dependents 50% graduate tuition waiver f or eligible employees in select programs Free access to WLU wellness facilities Free admission to athletic, cultural, and campus events with your Employee Topper Card The opportunity to make a lasting impact on students' educational journeys Additional Information For more information about living in the Wheeling area please visit Wheeling: Live Here - Weelunk West Liberty University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and welcomes applications from all interested individuals. Individuals who need assistance in the application process may contact Human Resources at hr@westliberty.edu. West Liberty University does not sponsor work visas. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States. Successfully passing a background screening report is required for final employment. West Liberty University is a tobacco free campus."
    },
    "https://westlibertyuniversity.bamboohr.com/careers/439": {
      "title": "Assistant Wrestling Coach",
      "description": "Assistant Wrestling Coach. Department: Administration & Staff Positions. Temporary. Assistant Wrestling Coach (Part-Time Temporary) West Liberty University | West Liberty, West Virginia Shape Champions. Build Leaders. Make an Impact. At West Liberty University , we believe athletics are an extension of the educational experience. As West Virginia's oldest institution of higher education, WLU provides students with exceptional academic opportunities, personalized support, and transformative experiences that prepare them for lifelong success. We are seeking a passionate, driven, and student-centered Assistant Wrestling Coach to join our Athletics team. This is an exciting opportunity for a coach who is committed to developing student-athletes both on the mat and in the classroom while contributing to the continued success and growth of our wrestling program. About the Position Reporting to the Head Wrestling Coach, the Assistant Wrestling Coach will play a key role in all aspects of a competitive collegiate wrestling program, including recruiting, coaching, player development, academic support, and program operations. The successful candidate will possess strong leadership skills, a commitment to NCAA compliance, and a passion for mentoring student-athletes. This position offers the opportunity to help build a championship-caliber program while positively impacting the lives of student-athletes through competition, academic achievement, and personal development. Position Type: Part-Time, Temporary Key Responsibilities Coaching & Athlete Development Assist with planning and conducting practices, training sessions, and competitions. Provide technical instruction and skill development for student-athletes. Help develop match strategies, scouting reports, and lineup decisions. Support strength and conditioning initiatives that enhance athletic performance. Recruitment & Retention Identify, evaluate, and recruit prospective student-athletes who align with the University's academic and athletic standards. Build relationships with high school, club, and collegiate coaches. Assist recruits through the admissions process and ensure timely submission of required documentation. Support student-athlete retention through ongoing mentorship and engagement. Academic & Student Success Monitor student-athlete academic performance, attendance, and progress toward degree completion. Promote a culture of academic excellence, accountability, and personal responsibility. Serve as a mentor and positive role model for student-athletes. Program Administration Assist with scheduling, travel preparation, equipment management, and program operations. Help manage equipment, uniforms, and supplies while maintaining budget awareness. Ensure compliance with all institutional, conference, and NCAA rules and regulations. Campus & Community Engagement Represent West Liberty University and the wrestling program with professionalism and integrity. Collaborate with athletics staff, campus partners, alumni, and community stakeholders. Participate in departmental meetings, events, and special projects as assigned. Serve on University committees and support broader institutional initiatives when requested. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Sports Management, Education, Exercise Science, or a related field. Minimum of one (1) year of coaching experience in wrestling at the high school, junior college, collegiate, club, or similar competitive level. Valid driver's license and ability to travel for recruiting and competition. Preferred Qualifications Collegiate wrestling coaching experience. Collegiate recruiting experience. Experience working with NCAA rules and compliance requirements. Demonstrated success in athlete development and program growth. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities The ideal candidate will demonstrate: Strong leadership, mentorship, and team-building abilities. Excellent verbal, written, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to recruit, motivate, and develop student-athletes. Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities simultaneously. Sound judgment, critical thinking, and problem-solving abilities. Commitment to fostering an inclusive and positive team culture. Proficiency with Microsoft Office and relevant athletics software systems. Ability to maintain confidentiality and professionalism in all aspects of the position. Why you should apply: Free use of the Wellness facilities and free admission into all WLU events with your employee Topper Card. For more information about living in the Wheeling area please visit Wheeling: Live Here - Weelunk West Liberty University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and welcomes applications from all interested individuals. Individuals who need assistance in the application process may contact Human Resources at hr@westliberty.edu. West Liberty University does not sponsor work visas. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States. Successfully passing a background screening report is required for final employment. West Liberty University is a tobacco free campus."
    },
    "https://westlibertyuniversity.bamboohr.com/careers/440": {
      "title": "Research Assistant",
      "description": "Research Assistant. Department: Administration & Staff Positions. Full-Time. Research Assistant – Two Positions Available West Liberty University | West Liberty, WV Join a Dynamic Biomedical Research Team West Liberty University is seeking applications for two full-time Research Assistant positions to support innovative biomedical research in a collaborative laboratory environment. This is an exciting opportunity for individuals who are passionate about scientific discovery and want to gain valuable hands-on experience working alongside faculty researchers and students. The successful candidates will play a key role in supporting laboratory operations, conducting experiments, maintaining research materials, and mentoring undergraduate researchers. This position offers an engaging environment where curiosity, collaboration, and attention to detail are highly valued. The Opportunity As a Research Assistant, you will contribute to ongoing biomedical research projects while helping maintain a productive and safe laboratory environment. You will work closely with faculty and students, gaining experience in experimental design, laboratory techniques, data analysis, and scientific research methodologies. Essential Responsibilities Conduct scientific experiments and accurately record, organize, and analyze research data. Manage laboratory inventory and coordinate the ordering of supplies and materials. Operate, maintain, and troubleshoot laboratory equipment, including microscopes, spectrometers, and centrifuges. Prepare laboratory media and maintain bacterial cultures and cell lines. Support undergraduate and graduate students in designing and conducting laboratory experiments. Maintain detailed laboratory notebooks and prepare graphs, tables, presentations, and research summaries as needed. Clean, sterilize, and maintain laboratory workspaces and equipment. Coordinate equipment maintenance and repairs when necessary. Ensure compliance with laboratory safety protocols and the proper handling and disposal of hazardous materials. Complete all required university training and safety modules. Perform other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Education Bachelor's degree in Biology, Biomedical Science, Biotechnology, Chemistry, Microbiology, or a closely related field required. Experience One to two years of laboratory, research, or related experience required. Preferred Skills & Abilities Successful candidates will demonstrate: Strong attention to detail and commitment to data accuracy Excellent organizational and time-management skills Effective written and verbal communication abilities A collaborative and team-oriented approach Integrity, professionalism, and dependability Ability to work independently while managing multiple priorities Interest in mentoring and supporting student researchers Why Join West Liberty University? At West Liberty University, you'll become part of a close-knit academic community dedicated to student success and scholarly achievement. Employees enjoy a variety of benefits and campus perks, including: Approximately two days of annual leave per month 12-13 paid holidays per year Comprehensive benefits package Free access to campus wellness facilities Free admission to WLU events with your employee Topper Card Educational benefits for employees and eligible family members: 100% undergraduate tuition waiver for eligible employees, spouses, and dependents 50% graduate tuition waiver for eligible employees in select programs Learn more about employee benefits: https://westliberty.edu/human-resources/employee-benefits Interested in relocating? Discover all that the Ohio Valley has to offer: https://weelunk.com/live-here/ Additional Information West Liberty University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and welcomes applications from all qualified individuals. Applicants requiring accommodations during the application process may contact Human Resources at hr@westliberty.edu . West Liberty University does not sponsor employment visas. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States. Final candidates must successfully complete a background screening. West Liberty University is a tobacco-free campus."
    },
    "https://westlibertyuniversity.bamboohr.com/careers/441": {
      "title": "Dean, College of Sciences",
      "description": "Dean, College of Sciences. Department: Administration & Staff Positions. Full-Time. INTERNAL SEARCH: Dean of the College of Sciences Shape the Future of Science Education at West Liberty University West Liberty University invites applications from qualified internal candidates for the position of Dean of the College of Sciences. This is an exciting leadership opportunity for a current WLU faculty member to help define the future of one of the University's largest and most dynamic academic colleges. Reporting directly to the Vice President for Academic Affairs , the Dean serves as the chief academic and administrative officer for the College of Sciences, providing vision, leadership, and strategic direction while fostering a culture of academic excellence, innovation, student success, and collaborative scholarship. This position is open to current West Liberty University employees only. External applications will not be considered. The College of Sciences includes the following academic departments and programs: Biological Sciences Communication Sciences and Disorders Medical Laboratory Science Psychology Physician Assistant Studies Nursing Dental Hygiene Physical Science and Mathematics The successful candidate will be a collaborative leader who is committed to advancing student achievement, supporting faculty excellence, strengthening academic programs, and building partnerships that enhance the College's impact both on campus and throughout the region. Key Leadership Responsibilities The Dean will: Provide visionary leadership and strategic direction for the College of Sciences. Lead the development, assessment, and continuous improvement of academic programs and curricula. Ensure successful accreditation outcomes and maintain productive relationships with accrediting and external agencies. Provide strategic leadership for enrollment growth, student retention, and student success initiatives across the College. Champion faculty and student engagement in research, scholarship, and creative activities. Foster excellence in teaching, innovation, and interdisciplinary collaboration. Manage college budgets, facilities, personnel, and resources effectively and responsibly. Develop annual budget requests in collaboration with department chairs and faculty. Make recommendations to the Vice President for Academic Affairs related to faculty recruitment, retention, promotion, tenure, evaluation, sabbatical leave, and disciplinary matters. Strengthen relationships with alumni, healthcare partners, industry leaders, and community organizations. Address faculty, staff, and student concerns with professionalism, fairness, and integrity. Support technology and instructional practices that enhance student engagement, retention, and degree completion. Perform additional duties as assigned by the Vice President for Academic Affairs. Minimum Qualifications Current West Liberty University employee. Minimum rank of Associate Professor at the time of appointment. Minimum of two years of full-time faculty experience . Demonstrated leadership experience in higher education, academic administration, committee leadership, program coordination, or related areas. Preferred Qualifications Earned doctoral degree in an appropriate discipline. Experience with accreditation processes, budget management, strategic planning, and personnel supervision. Evidence of successful collaboration across academic and administrative units. Desired Leadership Competencies The ideal candidate will demonstrate: Strategic Leadership Integrity and Ethical Decision-Making Collaboration and Relationship Building Initiative and Innovation Accountability and Dependability Strong Communication Skills Commitment to Student Success Sound Judgment and Problem-Solving Application Information This is an internal search and is open only to current West Liberty University employees. For full consideration, applications should be submitted by 13 November 2026 . West Liberty University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Individuals needing assistance with the application process may contact Human Resources at hr@westliberty.edu . Successful completion of a background check is required for final employment. West Liberty University is a tobacco-free campus. Why Join West Liberty University? At West Liberty University, you'll become part of a close-knit academic community dedicated to student success and scholarly achievement. Employees enjoy a variety of benefits and campus perks, including: Approximately two days of annual leave per month 12-13 paid holidays per year Comprehensive benefits package Free access to campus wellness facilities Free admission to WLU events with your employee Topper Card Educational benefits for employees and eligible family members: 100% undergraduate tuition waiver for eligible employees, spouses, and dependents 50% graduate tuition waiver for eligible employees in select programs Learn more about employee benefits: https://westliberty.edu/human-resources/employee-benefits Interested in relocating? Discover all that the Ohio Valley has to offer: https://weelunk.com/live-here/ Additional Information West Liberty University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and welcomes applications from all qualified individuals. Applicants requiring accommodations during the application process may contact Human Resources at hr@westliberty.edu . West Liberty University does not sponsor employment visas. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States. Final candidates must successfully complete a background screening. West Liberty University is a tobacco-free campus."
    },
    "https://westlibertyuniversity.bamboohr.com/careers/442": {
      "title": "Post-Doctorate Research Associate/ Lab Manager",
      "description": "Post-Doctorate Research Associate/ Lab Manager. Department: Administration & Staff Positions. Full-Time. Post-Doctorate Research Associate/ Lab Manager Hilltop Center for Biomedical Research | West Liberty University Anticipated Start Date: January 2027 Advance Biomedical Discovery. Mentor Future Scientists. Make an Impact. West Liberty University , West Virginia's oldest public university, invites applications for a Laboratory Research Scientist to join the Hilltop Center for Biomedical Research within the Department of Biology. This is an exciting opportunity for a passionate scientist to contribute to innovative, grant-funded biomedical research while helping shape the next generation of researchers. The successful candidate will join a collaborative team working in diverse areas of biomedical science, including: Microbial pathogenesis Antibiotic discovery and development Endocrine physiology Bone development and skeletal biology Funded through the West Virginia IDeA Network of Biomedical Research Excellence (WV-INBRE) , this position offers the opportunity to work alongside faculty investigators, mentor student researchers, and contribute to meaningful discoveries in a dynamic academic research environment. Position Responsibilities The Laboratory Research Scientist will play a key role in advancing ongoing research projects and supporting laboratory operations. Responsibilities include: Research Leadership Design, plan, conduct, troubleshoot, and analyze biomedical research experiments. Develop and optimize experimental protocols. Interpret and present scientific findings. Contribute to publications, reports, presentations, and grant-related activities. Student Mentorship Train and mentor undergraduate researchers. Guide students in laboratory techniques, experimental design, and data analysis. Foster best practices in research integrity, laboratory safety, and scientific professionalism. Laboratory Management Maintain laboratory organization and efficiency. Manage laboratory inventories, equipment, reagents, and supplies. Coordinate purchasing, maintenance, troubleshooting, and quality assurance activities. Oversee maintenance of microbial cultures, cell cultures, and biological stocks. Research Project Coordination Assist with managing multiple research projects simultaneously. Track milestones and research objectives. Coordinate resources, laboratory personnel, and project activities. Adapt research plans based on experimental findings and evolving priorities. Animal Research Support Coordinate and participate in approved animal research activities. Monitor animal health and maintain required records. Ensure compliance with institutional and regulatory standards. Qualifications Required Master's degree or doctoral degree in Biology, Biomedical Sciences, Molecular Biology, Physiology, Microbiology, or a closely related field. Minimum of 3-5 years of relevant laboratory research experience. Strong scientific writing and communication skills. Demonstrated knowledge of biomedical laboratory methodologies. Ability to work independently while contributing effectively within a collaborative team environment. Experience maintaining accurate laboratory records and research documentation. Preferred Ph.D. in a biomedical or related scientific discipline. Experience supervising or mentoring undergraduate or graduate researchers. Experience with cell culture, microbiological techniques, molecular biology, animal research, or related biomedical research methodologies. Experience in grant-funded research environments. Application Requirements: Letter of application Curriculum vitae Evidence of teaching effectiveness: course evaluations and sample syllabi Contact information for three professional references. This member is expected to participate in continuous improvement in the areas of teaching, professional development, and service to the University and community. Salary will be commensurate with experience. Why Join West Liberty University? At West Liberty University, you'll become part of a close-knit academic community dedicated to student success and scholarly achievement. Employees enjoy a variety of benefits and campus perks, including: Approximately two days of annual leave per month 12-13 paid holidays per year Comprehensive benefits package Free access to campus wellness facilities Free admission to WLU events with your employee Topper Card Educational benefits for employees and eligible family members: 100% undergraduate tuition waiver for eligible employees, spouses, and dependents 50% graduate tuition waiver for eligible employees in select programs 35% doctoral tuition waiver for eligible employees in select programs. Learn more about employee benefits: https://westliberty.edu/human-resources/employee-benefits Interested in relocating? Discover all that the Ohio Valley has to offer: https://weelunk.com/live-here/ Additional Information West Liberty University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and welcomes applications from all qualified individuals. Applicants requiring accommodations during the application process may contact Human Resources at hr@westliberty.edu . West Liberty University does not sponsor employment visas. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States. Final candidates must successfully complete a background screening. West Liberty University is a tobacco-free campus."
    }
  },
